From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:12:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] feat(iop): minimal libsd for IRX modules

Drivers that import libsd (CRI ADX's cri_adxi.irx, sndbase.irx) stream
through sceSdBlockTrans and wait for the transfer interrupt. There is no
sound yet: transfers drain at the SPU2's 48 kHz stereo rate and the
handler set with sceSdSetTransIntrHandler fires at each half buffer (loop
mode) or at the end (one-shot), so the drivers keep running.

Co-Authored-By: Lisvindanu <lisvindanu015@gmail.com>
